# This repository is a BUILT DISTRIBUTION, not source. Every file in it should come back out
# byte for byte identical to what went in, so nothing here gets its line endings rewritten.
#
# WHY IT MATTERS, with two examples that actually break:
#
#   jre/lib/jvm.cfg and jre/lib/tzmappings are read by the JVM itself at startup. They are
#   shipped with LF, and a checkout that helpfully turned them into CRLF would be handing the
#   runtime a config file in a shape it was never given.
#
#   FTCKesselRun.sh and FTCKesselRun.command are run by bash on macOS and Linux. A shell script
#   with CRLF fails with "bad interpreter: no such file or directory", which is the least
#   informative error in computing and has nothing to do with the interpreter.
#
# Git's default on Windows (core.autocrlf=true) does exactly that conversion, and it is right to
# for source. It is wrong for a folder that is meant to be a copy of a build.
* -text
